1. What incorrect result would integer division give for 137 / 8 before ceil() is applied?
It would result in 17 because C++ truncates the result. 
2. Why must the program convert at least one operand to a floating-point type?
So that it can perform floating-point division and keep its exact decimal value.
3. When does ceil() leave a value unchanged?
When it is already a whole number (Example 10.0)
